{"assets":["/statement-assets/2349bada8e832719ad5aa724d7d3c9295d239fc717a0675cf7f47641d3bc3460.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"436","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Feed with Candy"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The hero of the Cut the Rope game is a little monster named Om Nom. He loves candies. And what a coincidence! He also is the hero of today's problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/2349bada8e832719ad5aa724d7d3c9295d239fc717a0675cf7f47641d3bc3460.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One day, Om Nom visited his friend Evan. Evan has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" candies of two types (fruit drops and caramel drops), the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th candy hangs at the height of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"hi"},{"kind":"text","text":" centimeters above the floor of the house, its mass is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"mi"},{"kind":"text","text":". Om Nom wants to eat as many candies as possible. At the beginning Om Nom can make at most "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" centimeter high jumps. When Om Nom eats a candy of mass "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":", he gets stronger and the height of his jump increases by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" centimeters."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What maximum number of candies can Om Nom eat if he never eats two candies of the same type in a row (Om Nom finds it too boring)?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n, x ≤ 2000)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of sweets Evan has and the initial height of Om Nom's jump. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti, hi, mi"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0 ≤ ti ≤ 1; 1 ≤ hi, mi ≤ 2000)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the type, height and the mass of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th candy. If number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals 0, then the current candy is a caramel drop, otherwise it is a fruit drop."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single integer — the maximum number of candies Om Nom can eat."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 3\n0 2 4\n1 3 1\n0 8 3\n0 20 10\n1 5 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One of the possible ways to eat "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" candies is to eat them in the order: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's assume the following scenario:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Initially, the height of Om Nom's jump equals "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":". He can reach candies "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's assume that he eats candy "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". As the mass of this candy equals "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":", the height of his jump will rise to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 + 4 = 7"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Now Om Nom can reach candies "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's assume that he eats candy "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then the height of his jump will be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"7 + 5 = 12"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" At this moment, Om Nom can reach two candies, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":". He won't eat candy "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" as its type matches the type of the previously eaten candy. Om Nom eats candy "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":", the height of his jump is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"12 + 3 = 15"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Om Nom eats candy "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":", the height of his jump is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"15 + 1 = 16"},{"kind":"text","text":". He cannot reach candy "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"436A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/436/problem/A"}